arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: name the panel after the machine, not a guess

Two panel variants ship on identical wiring, so the compatible cannot
honestly name a controller. Use "planet,gemini-panel"; the driver decides
which panel is fitted from the identity LK publishes.

Signed-off-by: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -880,11 +880,15 @@
 	#size-cells = <0>;
 
 	/*
-	 * Solomon SSD2092 FHD panel on DSI0 (LK: aeon_ssd2092_fhd_dsi_solomon,
-	 * panel ID 0x01572098 — probed by the stock bootloader at every boot).
+	 * The Gemini's FHD 1080x2160 DSI panel. Deliberately NOT named after a
+	 * controller: two variants shipped on identical wiring (Novatek
+	 * NT36672 and Solomon SSD2092) and the board cannot tell you which is
+	 * fitted. The driver asks LK, which probes it at every boot and
+	 * publishes the LCM name in /chosen/atag,videolfb — on this unit,
+	 * "aeon_nt36672_fhd_dsi_vdo_x600_xinli".
 	 */
-	panel@0 {
-		compatible = "solomon,ssd2092";
+	gemini_panel: panel@0 {
+		compatible = "planet,gemini-panel";
 		reg = <0>;
 		avdd-supply = <&lcd_avdd>;
 		avee-supply = <&lcd_avee>;
